/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1115:\section{Proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:main_technical_theorem}}\label{sec:spreadness_frm_vertex_spreadness}
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1117:In this section, we prove Theorem~\ref{thm:main_technical_theorem}.
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1118:%by using Proposition~\ref{prop:vertex_to_edge} and the FKNP theorem. 
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1130:\begin{theorem}\cite[Theorem 3.1]{han2020complexity}\label{thm:han_structural_theorem}
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1146:We are now ready to prove Theorem~\ref{thm:main_technical_theorem}, 
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1147:using Theorem~\ref{thm:han_structural_theorem} as a key tool.
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1150:\begin{proof}[Proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:main_technical_theorem}]
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1157:The main task of this proof is to define $\psi:G\hookrightarrow H$, a random embedding of an $F$-factor in $H$, and we achieve it in a few steps.
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1165:Our goal is to apply Theorem \ref{thm:han_structural_theorem} to each random cluster and obtain an $F$-factor in each of them.
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1184:\begin{proof}
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1193:\end{proof}
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1212:        We claim that $H_i$ and $ \mathcal{P}^{H_i}$ satisfy the properties described in Theorem \ref{thm:han_structural_theorem}. By applying Theorem \ref{thm:han_structural_theorem} to $ H_i$ and $ \mathcal{P}^{H_i}$, we obtain an $F$-factor $ M_2^i $ in $H_i$. 
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1228:        Therefore, for $i\in [m]$, each $H_i$ equipped with partition $\mathcal P_i$ satisfies the assumptions of Theorem \ref{thm:han_structural_theorem}, and thus has an $F$-factor.
/tmp/tmp.i55aPydxD9/main.tex:1234:        Now we are ready to define the random embedding function and conclude the proof.
