+NOTES = r"""
+Paper grounding. Section 1.1 defines k-uniform hypergraphs, matchings, perfect
+matchings, minimum l-degree, and PM(k,l,delta). Theorem 1.2 says that above the
+perfect-fractional-matching threshold the dense decision problem is in P and
+even outputs a perfect matching or a negative certificate. Theorem 1.4 extends
+that tractable regime to random sparsifications. These positive results make a
+Track A claim in the paper's main dense regime untenable.
