-k-sets avoiding s whose good-tag count is even. Their index vectors generate
-L={z: sum(z)=0 mod k and z_G=0 mod 2}. The total number of vertices is a multiple
-of k and the good-tag part has odd size. Deleting E(x) therefore leaves an index
-vector in L exactly when E(x) carries a G tag.
 
