+all p+1 projective starts, O(g+p); it succeeds and is reported separately as the
+Track B reference algorithm. At the shipping preset it performs 1,000,004
+fixed-point tests plus 96 elementary matrix operations. The compact route uses
+the same cyclic product but recognizes its parabolic conjugacy type and extracts
+the double fixed point directly, then propagates the answer, for at most 148
+field operations. The former is easy for a computer but not executable by hand;
+the latter is short if the invariant is noticed.
+
+Attacks. Per-coordinate exceptional incidence is exactly one, so the outlier
+probe has only a label tie and chooses zero. Zero-start propagation is wrong by
+construction. Uniform 256-restart sampling is tested against the exact bounded
+certificate language. The in-context affine ansatz replaces each projective map
+by the affine map agreeing at 0 and 1, solves that easier cycle, and then checks
+the resulting true trajectory; conditioned instances defeat it. The exact
+fixed-point scan succeeds as expected and is not placed among failing Track B
+attacks.
+
+Canonicalization. Independent projective relabellings of coordinate parts
+conjugate adjacent matrices; cyclic rotations and reversals reorder/invert the
+cycle. Coordinate-part padding sizes are genuine partition data but independent
+of the planted start. The key uses their sorted multiset together with the field
+and fixed part sizes, so it is invariant under these transformations and does
+not use the seed, answer, public coefficients, or rendered text. It is a strong
+cheap invariant for the succinct decorated hypergraph, not a complete
+canonization under every abstract hypergraph isomorphism.
+""".strip()
+
+
+_ANSWER_RE = re.compile(r"<answer\b[^>]*>(.*?)</answer\s*>", re.I | re.S)
+_FENCE_RE = re.compile(r"```(?:json|text)?\s*(.*?)```", re.I | re.S)
+_ENUMERATION_CAP = 200_000
